.TH XCTEST 1 2026-11-09 "tools-xctest" "GNUstep"
.SH NAME
xctest \- run the XCTest tests in a test bundle
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xctest
.RI [ options ]
.I bundle
.br
.B xctest
.B \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xctest
loads
.IR bundle ,
a test bundle (usually
.IR Name.xctest ),
finds the
.B XCTestCase
subclasses in it, and runs their test methods.
Results are logged as they run, followed by a summary that lists the failed
tests.
.PP
The bundle's name without its extension is the
.IR "test target" .
Tests are named by identifiers of the form
.IR TestTarget [/ TestClass [/ testMethod ]].
.PP
Options may come before or after
.IR bundle .
.B YES
and
.B NO
may be written in any case.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Selecting tests
.TP
.BI \-only\-testing: identifier
Run only the tests matching
.IR identifier ,
which is
.IR TestTarget ,
.IR TestTarget/TestClass
or
.IR TestTarget/TestClass/testMethod .
May be given more than once.
.TP
.BI \-skip\-testing: identifier
Skip the tests matching
.IR identifier .
May be given more than once, and combined with
.BR \-only\-testing .
.TP
.BI \-XCTest " tests"
Apple's selection syntax:
.B All
for every test, or a comma-separated list of
.IR Class ,
.I Class/method
or
.IR Class.method .
.PP
Each selection given by
.B \-only\-testing
or
.B \-XCTest
must match at least one test, or
.B xctest
fails without running any; a
.B \-skip\-testing
that matches nothing is ignored.
.SS Listing tests
.TP
.B \-list\-tests
Print the selected tests, one identifier per line, without running them.
.TP
.B \-list\-tests\-json
Print the selected tests as JSON, without running them.
.SS Output and reports
.TP
.BI \-output\-format " format"
.B classic
(the default) logs results as
.B XCTest:
lines.
.B apple
prints them on standard output in the format of Apple's
.BR xctest ,
with per-test timings, for tools that parse it.
.TP
.BI \-junit\-report " path"
Also write the results to
.I path
as JUnit XML: one
.B <testsuite>
per test class, with assertion failures as
.BR <failure> ,
uncaught exceptions as
.B <error>
and skipped tests as
.BR <skipped> .
.TP
.BI \-attachments\-path " dir"
Save test attachments under
.IR dir .
By default they are saved next to the
.B \-junit\-report
file, in
.IR report \-attachments.
.SS Hosted tests
.TP
.BI \-host " app"
Run the tests inside an application,
.I app
being a
.I .app
bundle or an executable.
.B xctest
launches it with
.B libXCTestHost
preloaded, and the tests run on its main thread once it has finished
launching.
Not supported on Windows.
.TP
.BI \-host\-launch\-timeout " seconds"
Stop the application and fail if it hasn't started the tests within
.I seconds
(default 60; 0 waits forever).
The tests themselves have no time limit.
.SS Performance tests
.TP
.BI \-performance\-baselines " path"
Fail a measured test whose average is worse than its baseline in the JSON file
.I path
by more than the baseline's
.B maxPercentRegression
(default 10%).
.TP
.B \-update\-performance\-baselines
Record the measured averages into the
.B \-performance\-baselines
file.
.TP
.BI \-performance\-warmup\-iterations " n"
Unmeasured runs before each measurement.
By default there are none for
.BR measureBlock: ,
and one for
.BR measureWithMetrics: .
.TP
.BI \-performance\-report " path"
Also write every measurement of the run to
.I path
as JSON, with its statistics, its baseline and the verdict.
.TP
.BI \-performance\-machine\-id " id"
Use, and record, the baselines for machine
.IR id .
.B auto
names the machine by its CPU, number of cores and architecture.
The default is
.BR XCTEST_MACHINE_ID .
.TP
.BR \-performance\-inconclusive\-fails " YES|NO"
Fail a test whose comparison with its baseline is inconclusive.
The default,
.BR NO ,
only reports it.
.SS Repetition
.TP
.BI \-test\-iterations " n"
Run each test
.I n
times.
With either option below,
.I n
is the most times a test runs.
.TP
.B \-run\-tests\-until\-failure
Repeat each test until it fails, at most 100 times unless
.B \-test\-iterations
says otherwise.
.TP
.B \-retry\-tests\-on\-failure
Retry a failing test until it passes, at most 3 times unless
.B \-test\-iterations
says otherwise.
Failed attempts followed by a pass don't count as failures.
.PP
Each run uses a new test case instance; a class's
.B +setUp
and
.B +tearDown
still run once.
.SS Order
.TP
.BI \-test\-execution\-order " order"
.B alphabetical
(the default) or
.BR random ,
which shuffles the test classes, and the tests within each class.
The seed is logged and recorded in the JUnit report.
.TP
.BI \-test\-execution\-order\-seed " n"
Repeat the random order given by seed
.IR n .
Implies
.BR "\-test\-execution\-order random" .
.SS Parallel testing
.TP
.BR \-parallel\-testing\-enabled " YES|NO"
Run each test class in a separate
.B xctest
worker process (default
.BR NO ).
Each class's output is printed as one block when it finishes.
A worker that crashes fails only its own class's tests.
Can't be combined with
.BR \-host .
.TP
.BI \-parallel\-testing\-worker\-count " n"
Run
.I n
workers at once (default: one per CPU).
Implies
.BR "\-parallel\-testing\-enabled YES" .
.SS Time limits
.TP
.BR \-test\-timeouts\-enabled " YES|NO"
Fail a test, including its set up and tear down, that runs longer than its
.BR executionTimeAllowance ,
then stop the run without running the remaining tests (default
.BR NO ).
.TP
.BI \-default\-test\-execution\-time\-allowance " seconds"
Each test's allowance, unless the test sets its own (default 600).
Implies
.BR "\-test\-timeouts\-enabled YES" .
.TP
.BI \-maximum\-test\-execution\-time\-allowance " seconds"
The most any test's allowance may be.
Implies
.BR "\-test\-timeouts\-enabled YES" .
.SS Help
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a summary of the options and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
At least one test ran, and every selected test succeeded; or the tests were
listed; or help was printed.
.TP
.B 1
Anything else: a test failed or raised an uncaught exception, no test ran, a
selection matched no test, the bundle couldn't be loaded, a test ran out of
time, or an option was unknown or invalid.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XCTEST_MACHINE_ID
The machine's name for performance baselines, when
.B \-performance\-machine\-id
isn't given.
.TP
.B XCTEST_PERF_COUNTERS
Set to
.B 0
to turn off the hardware performance counters (Linux only).
.TP
.B XCTEST_HOST_LIBRARY
The
.B libXCTestHost
library that
.B \-host
preloads, instead of the one installed beside
.BR libXCTest .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $GNUSTEP_MAKEFILES/Auxiliary/xctest.make
Builds test bundles with gnustep-make.
Name them in
.BR XCTEST_BUNDLE_NAME ;
.B make check
runs them with
.BR xctest ,
passing it
.BR XCTEST_FLAGS .
See the comments at the top of the file.
.TP
.B xctest\-bundle
.I Name.xctest library
.RI [ class ]
.br
Wraps a shared library of tests as a bundle that
.B xctest
can load, for build systems other than gnustep-make, such as Meson.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run every test in a bundle:
.PP
.RS
.EX
xctest MyTests.xctest
.EE
.RE
.PP
Run one class, and one test of another, with Apple's selection syntax:
.PP
.RS
.EX
xctest \-XCTest FooTests,BarTests/testParse MyTests.xctest
.EE
.RE
.PP
Skip a slow class and write a JUnit report for CI:
.PP
.RS
.EX
xctest \-skip\-testing:MyTests/SlowTests \-junit\-report results.xml MyTests.xctest
.EE
.RE
.PP
Check what a filter selects, without running anything:
.PP
.RS
.EX
xctest \-list\-tests \-only\-testing:MyTests/FooTests MyTests.xctest
.EE
.RE
.PP
Look for order-dependent tests, in parallel:
.PP
.RS
.EX
xctest \-test\-execution\-order random \-parallel\-testing\-enabled YES MyTests.xctest
.EE
.RE
.PP
Run the tests inside an application, on a headless machine:
.PP
.RS
.EX
xvfb\-run \-a xctest \-host MyApp.app MyAppTests.xctest
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR make (1),
.BR buildtool (1)
.PP
The README of tools-xctest describes the supported XCTest API.
